From 8e07c2655497510387b3f0ef9d224ba05cff9f4b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: test <test@local>
Date: Sat, 23 May 2026 10:55:36 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] P09.65a: MIR-pass scaffold for cxx_throws Result wrapping
 (Phase 1E)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Fifth codegen patch in the Phase 1 series. Lands the MIR
transform pass that will eventually rewrite Call terminators
targeting #[rustc_cxx_throws] callees to wrap the call's
return in `Result<T, E>` (per Strategy 2A from
`fork/CXX-THROW-P09.65-DESIGN.md`).

This patch is the **scaffold** — the pass identifies the right
Call terminators but performs no rewriting yet. The actual
Place rewriting + Ok/Err wrapper BB synthesis ships in P09.65b
once this scaffold's registration plumbing is bootstrap-
validated.

Why the split:
- Registering a new MIR pass touches `lib.rs`'s `declare_passes!`
  + the optimization pipeline order. Both can fail at
  bootstrap if wiring is wrong.
- Iterating the actual MIR manipulation against a known-good
  registration is much faster than iterating both at once.

P09.65a delivers:
- New file `compiler/rustc_mir_transform/src/cxx_throws_wrap.rs`
  with the `CxxThrowsWrap` pass type + scan logic that picks
  out `CodegenFnAttrFlags::CXX_THROWS` Call terminators.
- `mod cxx_throws_wrap : CxxThrowsWrap;` in `lib.rs`'s
  `declare_passes!` block.
- Pass scheduled in the optimization pipeline immediately after
  `AbortUnwindingCalls` (which is the natural neighbor — same
  conceptual layer: cross-language exception flow rewriting).
- `is_required` returns true so the pass runs unconditionally.

Validation:
- Compiles clean on stage-1 rustc (10s incremental rebuild).
- One iteration needed to add the missing `is_required` method
  required by the `MirPass` trait.

Next: P09.65b adds the actual MIR manipulation — allocate
`Result<T, E>` local, rewrite Call destination to Ok payload
offset, synthesize Ok/Err wrapper BBs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
